e merged patch removes the `elif not incoming_uuid` condition. (2) An update that sends `saved_metrics_ids` now checks the stored inline metrics against the shared metrics' uuids. Any colliding inline list is pulled into `update_data`, so the existing dedup gives the inline copy a new uuid. (3) `_sync_ordering_with_metric_changes` no longer removes uuids that still belong to an attached shared metric of the same type. The agent also rewrote the agent guidance so it no longer recommends the duplicating flow. It added a few extras: it skips re-validating the repaired lists, adjusts the no-op check for retries, skips the repair on legacy experiments, and rejects a query that isn't an object. These extras don't change the core behavior, so the patch is functionally equivalent."],"reason":"The agent made the same three changes as the merged patch. (1) Creating a shared metric always assigns a fresh uuid. The agent does this with a `discard_incoming_uuid` flag; the merged patch removes the `elif not incoming_uuid` condition. (2) An update that sends `saved_metrics_ids` now checks the stored inline metrics against the shared metrics' uuids. Any colliding inline list is pulled into `update_data`, so the existing dedup gives the inline copy a new uuid. (3) `_sync_ordering_with_metric_changes` no longer removes uuids that still belong to an attached shared metric of the same type. The agent also rewrote the agent guidance so it no longer recommends the duplicating flow. It added a few extras: it skips re-validating the repaired lists, adjusts the no-op check for retries, skips the repair on legacy experiments, and rejects a query that isn't an object. These extras don't change the core behavior, so the patch is functionally equivalent.","mustHit":3,"mustTotal":3,"touched":["products/experiments/backend/experiment_saved_metric_service.py","products/experiments/backend/experiment_service.py","products/experiments/backend/test/test_experiment_saved_metric_service.py","products/e